1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:09,890
Every observation begins as an experience.

2
00:00:13,090 --> 00:00:19,603
Your perception is formed from sensory data.

3
00:00:20,703 --> 00:00:27,328
The sensory apparatus is not the whole story.

4
00:00:31,128 --> 00:00:34,862
[DOT proposes] You are Little c.

5
00:00:35,962 --> 00:00:40,577
[DOT proposes] The body is your interface.

6
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:51,932
[The prevailing view] “You’re nothing but a pack of neurons.” — Francis Crick, The Astonishing Hypothesis, 1994

7
00:00:53,032 --> 00:01:00,215
Yet experience itself stays outside the equations.

8
00:01:03,815 --> 00:01:10,775
We map the world in detail; ourselves, far less.

9
00:01:11,875 --> 00:01:19,282
Others fill the gap: markets, platforms, ideologies.

10
00:01:21,682 --> 00:01:28,195
The body protests: stress, anxiety, burnout.

11
00:01:29,295 --> 00:01:35,473
We treat the signal more than its source.

12
00:01:36,573 --> 00:01:43,533
The costs compound: division, despair, conflict.

13
00:01:44,633 --> 00:01:50,700
At root, this is a problem of knowledge.

14
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:59,115
Notice who is experiencing.

15
00:02:00,215 --> 00:02:06,058
Test this against your own experience.

16
00:02:23,658 --> 00:02:36,000
Digital Organism Theory

17
00:02:26,292 --> 00:02:36,000
A pragmatic, testable framework for experience.

18
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:49,400
Concept 1 of 17 · The Subjective Data Principle
Feeling must be treated as data, but feeling is not automatically truth.

19
00:02:50,400 --> 00:03:05,400
Concept 2 of 17 · Digital Organism
A living, conscious system that carries its past forward, senses what matters, and adapts to stay whole across change.

20
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:24,400
Concept 3 of 17 · The Big C Hypothesis
Consciousness is fundamental: the larger living awareness—emerged within T × E—from which worlds and individual minds arise.

21
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:44,400
Concept 4 of 17 · Little c
You as an individual center of awareness: experiencing the world through a body, choosing, and growing through what happens next.

22
00:03:45,400 --> 00:04:00,400
Concept 5 of 17 · The Decoupling Principle
Your awareness and your body work closely together—without your body being all that you are.

23
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:17,400
Concept 6 of 17 · Reality Frame
A shared world with stable rules where actions have real, learnable consequences.

24
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:35,400
Concept 7 of 17 · Physical Sciences as Frame Derivations
Physics measures the reliable rules of our world (RF₀); DOT asks why a world for learning needs rules that hold.

25
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:55,400
Concept 8 of 17 · Reality Stream
Your personal stream of moments: how our shared world reaches you from where you stand.

26
00:04:56,400 --> 00:05:08,400
Concept 9 of 17 · Intent
The inner turning point where one passing thought becomes what you actually commit to do.

27
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:25,400
Concept 10 of 17 · The Experience Loop
A moment arrives, your past lens interprets it, you choose an action, and the result reshapes you for next time.

28
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:40,400
Concept 11 of 17 · Canvas
The deep inner record that holds every mark experience leaves on you across your life.

29
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:54,400
Concept 12 of 17 · Painting
The lens of beliefs, fears, and expectations you have built so far—coloring every new moment before you think.

30
00:05:55,400 --> 00:06:07,400
Concept 13 of 17 · Character
The automatic version of you that runs on habit when you repeat the same reactions over and over.

31
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:20,400
Concept 14 of 17 · The Fear-Gating Principle
When Fear governs, the set of responses that feels available becomes narrower.

32
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:35,400
Ego defends the Character Little c has learned to call itself.
To protect its fears, Little c paints Ego around the body—and when Ego hardens into Arrogance, it blocks new experience from changing the Canvas.

33
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:48,400
Concept 15 of 17 · Love as an Epistemic Condition
Love is the condition in which Fear no longer governs you.

34
00:06:49,400 --> 00:07:04,400
Concept 16 of 17 · Conscious Authorship
See the Painting, widen the pause before Intent, and choose what the next consequence will reinforce.

35
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:20,400
Concept 17 of 17 · Limits and Unpaid Debts
Every claim is labeled—observed, modeled, hypothesized, or speculative—so this never becomes a blind belief system.
